 "_note_brand": "A name's own Latin spelling, taken from a record in this catalogue that carries it. Used where a state register writes a name in Thai and the building's own sign writes it in Latin: ปันนา read by the letter rules is Panna, and three mapped buildings on this same shelf spell it Punna. The claim is about SPELLING only — never that one owner holds them all, which nothing on this disk states. Each entry names the record the spelling was read from.",
 "_brand_source": "each spelling read off a record in data/canonical on the same shelf, 2026-09-04 (WO-56)",
 "_sweep_2026_09_04": "WO-56 swept every shelf, not only housing. Entries were found by comparing our reading against the HUMAN English name held on the same record (4,894 records carry both) and keeping only pairs that share a consonant shape — a transliteration. Pairs that do not were left alone on purpose: กาแฟ→Coffee and เภสัช→Pharmacy are TRANSLATIONS, the readings Kafae and Phesat are correct, and a translation belongs in the search index's matched-never-shown words, not in a romanisation.",
 "_note_loanword_2026_09_06": "Trade-tag loanwords added 2026-09-06 while building data/trade_lexicon.json (importers/build_trade_lexicon.py): the words a repair shop's own tags are written in — มอเตอร์ไซค์, แอร์, คอมพิวเตอร์ — which the letter rules read to nothing or to noise. English written in Thai script; the reading IS the English.",
 "_note_2026_09_07": "Four Pali/Sanskrit forms (อุโบสถ, สุรพงษ์, อากาศยาน, หฤทัย) whose sandhi the syllable rules cannot reach, and three ทับศัพท์ (Hill, Place) read off shop signs in the catalogue — found by a 30-name random sample of the live index (WO-72).",
 "_note_2026_09_08": "แก้ว, นวรัฐ and ได้รับ, found while WO-77 measured what the pages print. แก้ว read 'Kwae' (the ว taken as the second half of a กว cluster rather than the final /o/) and นวรัฐ read 'Norat' (the unwritten vowel between น and ว dropped), so ถ.แก้วนวรัฐ — a road you can see from Nawarat Bridge — read 'Kwaenorat'. ได้รับ read 'Draiba': ดร is a loanword cluster and this is ได้ + รับ. All three are shapes the letter rules cannot decide, which is what this file is for.",
 "_note_2026_09_08_irregular": "Seven forms found by measuring translit.romanize against pythainlp/thai-romanization-dataset (CC-BY-SA-3.0, 498,966 word pairs) — the first time this file's output had been checked against an outside corpus. เกษตร, เพชร and ถาวร are Sanskrit loans whose written vowel is not said where it is written (kṣetra is ka-set, not ke-set), which is what this section is for; they were read ketta, phetra and thaora, and 739 records in data/canonical carry one of them — เพชรเกษม, a national highway, read 'phetraketma'. จอดรถ is different in kind: the syllable walker leaves ด to open a syllable instead of closing จอด, giving a voiced d Thai has no final for. A rule fix for that was tried and MEASURED WORSE (-187 words on the corpus) so it was reverted; the entry is here because the walker's choice between a final and a new syllable is not a thing one lookahead can settle. แหน was left alone on purpose: it is genuinely two words — /nae/ with a silent leading ห as in จอกแหน, and /haen/ as in หวงแหน — so neither reading is the correct one.",
 "_note_loanword_2026_10_05": "Shop-sign loanwords added 2026-10-05 after Nan graded the portrait of เรื่องของผม บาร์เบอร์ 0: บาร์เบอร์ read 'Bar boe', and a reader took the place for a bar. Candidates were counted against the Thai names in data/canonical and kept where they occur; every reading that changed (about 3,000 names) was sampled per entry. Short entries join the segmenter's dictionary, so each was checked for words it cuts into: เทค was dropped (it split เทควันโด and เทคโน), and คัทลียา, เน็ตเวิร์ค and แคมป์ปิ้ง are here because คัท, เน็ต and แคมป์ cut them. ชาบู, ปั๊ม, ไปรษณีย์ and other Thai or non-English words were left to the letter rules.",
 "_note_loanword_2026_10_11": "ทอป, ท็อป, ท๊อป = Top: Nan 2026-10-11, of โรงแรมทอปนอร์ท ('Top North Hotel, like the sign in the picture says'), which read 'Thop North'. Same day, thapsap mine + export added the loanwords newly aligned from records carrying both names (thapsap export's own production gate). Five of that export's additions removed on reading them (สาขาเชียงใหม่ had become 'Music Arms Chiang Mai'); marked rejected in thapsap's catalog so a later export leaves them out."
}